= BITwiki Charter =

The BITwiki Charter defines the public purpose and scope of the project.

== Mission ==
Build a durable, inspectable knowledge system in which useful information can be structured, sourced, related, revised, transcluded, and reused by humans and machines.

== Commitments ==
* Preserve source fidelity while improving organization and clarity.
* Prefer evidence, provenance, and explicit uncertainty over unsupported certainty.
* Keep ontology, epistemology, and axiology distinct but connected.
* Use native MediaWiki semantics before inventing new abstractions.
* Keep knowledge modular and composable without sacrificing coherent canonical pages.
* Preserve revision history and continuity through redirects rather than duplicate FINAL/REVISED copies.
* Distinguish public knowledge from protected or private memory.
* Keep public Git representations public-safe.
* Treat AI as an assisting participant whose outputs remain reviewable and attributable.

== Scope ==
BITwiki may contain encyclopedia content, research synthesis, concepts, theories, projects, implementations, publications, datasets, technical documentation, public ecosystem documentation, and other durable knowledge objects.

== Non-goals ==
BITwiki is not a filesystem simulation, a dumping ground for every interaction, or a claim that all included perspectives are equally evidenced.

